# Copy to .env.local and adjust for your setup.

# Base URL the browser uses to fetch artwork variants (pre-built AVIF/WebP
# files + originals). Defaults (in code) to the rclone HTTP server run by
# the asset HTTP server (scripts/serve-assets.mjs) on :9837. Override to
# point at R2, a public CDN, or any other HTTP file host.
NEXT_PUBLIC_ASSETS_BASE_URL=http://localhost:9837

# Canonical site URL (used for artwork links in the email and absolute URLs
# in metadata / sitemaps / JSON-LD). Falls back to a hardcoded prod URL
# (or localhost in dev) if unset.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=https://collection-of-beauty.example.com

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Newsletter (ListMonk + Amazon SES, provisioned by Hatchkit)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Editions live as markdown under content/newsletter/. There is no cron
# job and no /api/newsletter/send route. Sending happens via the CLI:
#   pnpm newsletter:send <slug>             # dry-run, .env.development
#   pnpm newsletter:send <slug> --confirm   # test list, .env.development
#   NODE_ENV=production pnpm newsletter:send <slug> --confirm  # live, .env.production
# The wrapper at scripts/newsletter-send.sh picks the env file based on
# NODE_ENV. Both env files use the SAME variable name `LISTMONK_LIST_ID`
# with different numeric values — the runtime never branches on NODE_ENV
# for list selection.
#
# Architecture:
#   - ListMonk holds subscribers + list memberships + dispatches sends.
#   - ListMonk is configured (by Hatchkit, in its admin settings) to
#     deliver via Amazon SES SMTP. The SES_* env vars below are emitted
#     by Hatchkit but the runtime only reads `SES_FROM_EMAIL` (as the
#     campaign from-address fallback when `LISTMONK_FROM` is unset).
#   - The app talks to ListMonk's HTTP API: it adds subscribers for the
#     double-opt-in form, sends transactional confirmation emails
#     through /api/tx, and triggers the weekly digest via /api/campaigns.
#
# What Hatchkit provisions automatically (via `hatchkit provision`):
#   - Two ListMonk lists (prod + dev), each with a unique numeric id.
#   - An API user with the right permissions.
#   - SES SMTP wired into ListMonk's Settings → SMTP.
#   - The following env vars rendered into .env.production / .env.development:
#       LISTMONK_URL
#       LISTMONK_API_USER
#       LISTMONK_API_TOKEN
#       LISTMONK_LIST_ID         (different value per env file)
#       SES_SMTP_HOST, SES_SMTP_PORT, SES_SMTP_USERNAME, SES_SMTP_PASSWORD
#       SES_FROM_EMAIL
#       SES_REGION
#
# What still has to be done by hand (one-time):
#   - The two passthrough templates the app needs. Run
#     `pnpm listmonk:bootstrap` to create them idempotently — the script
#     prints two ids that go into LISTMONK_TX_TEMPLATE_ID and
#     LISTMONK_CAMPAIGN_TEMPLATE_ID in both env files.

# ── Hatchkit-emitted (do not edit by hand, refresh with hatchkit) ──
# LISTMONK_URL=https://listmonk.example.com
# LISTMONK_API_USER=
# LISTMONK_API_TOKEN=
# LISTMONK_LIST_ID=1
# SES_FROM_EMAIL=noreply@mail.beauty.example.com
# SES_SMTP_HOST=email-smtp.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com
# SES_SMTP_PORT=587
# SES_SMTP_USERNAME=
# SES_SMTP_PASSWORD=
# SES_REGION=eu-west-1

# ── App-specific, set after `pnpm listmonk:bootstrap` ──
# LISTMONK_TX_TEMPLATE_ID=
# LISTMONK_CAMPAIGN_TEMPLATE_ID=

# ── Optional display-name override (defaults to SES_FROM_EMAIL above) ──
# LISTMONK_FROM="A Drop of Beauty <hello@beauty.example.com>"

# Optional public asset host override for email images. Leave unset for
# local dev unless you need a different bucket/CDN; email clients cannot
# load localhost URLs, so newsletter email images fall back to the
# deployed assets bucket.
# NEWSLETTER_ASSETS_BASE_URL=https://assets.beauty.trebeljahr.com

# HMAC secret for the double-opt-in confirmation tokens issued by
# /api/newsletter/subscribe. Generate with: openssl rand -hex 32
# NEWSLETTER_TOKEN_SECRET=

# Cloudflare R2 credentials — public assets bucket only (no state file
# any more; newsletter "has it been sent" lives in git via the markdown
# files in content/newsletter/).
# R2_ENDPOINT=https://<account-id>.r2.cloudflarestorage.com
# R2_ACCESS_KEY_ID=
# R2_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=

# Pre-built variant assets (AVIF/WebP) for the production site. Public-read,
# served directly to browsers. Sync with `pnpm assets:sync` after every
# `pnpm shrink`. Set NEXT_PUBLIC_ASSETS_BASE_URL above to this bucket's
# public URL (R2 dev URL or a custom domain) for prod builds.
# R2_ASSETS_BUCKET=collection-of-beauty-assets
